"The dropped “tf394kv.dll” file is an external C&C communications library, compiled on July 24th, 2015 and used by the main backdoor for all Internet-based communications. The module aborts the thread receiving C2 command after it fails to correctly execute commands more than six times in a row, i.e. if file or process creation fails. The export called “SendDataToServer_2” does exactly what the name means: it encrypts all collected data, encodes it using Base64 encoding and calls its additional library to send the data to the C2 server. Targeted sectors: Defense, Financial, Government, Transport. Delivery method(s): email, usb, website. Tools/frameworks observed: cmd, mimikatz, powershell, rundll32.",APT28,gold,cyber,G0007,Turla,203c6e1a0264
"The dropped “tf394kv.dll” file is an external C&C communications library, compiled on July 24th, 2015 and used by the main backdoor for all Internet-based communications. The module aborts the thread receiving C2 command after it fails to correctly execute commands more than six times in a row, i.e. if file or process creation fails. The export called “SendDataToServer_2” does exactly what the name means: it encrypts all collected data, encodes it using Base64 encoding and calls its additional library to send the data to the C2 server. Targeted sectors: Defense, Financial, Government, Transport. Delivery method(s): email, usb, website. Tools/frameworks observed: cmd, mimikatz, powershell, rundll32.",Turla,distractor,cyber,G0007,Turla,203c6e1a0264
"To execute the dropped DLL, the [REDACTED_MALWARE] first checks the integrity level of the executing process, and if it does not have the necessary permissions, the [REDACTED_MALWARE] will enumerate the system’s processes searching for explorer.exe. To carry out C2 communications via injected code in a remote process, the injected code reaches out to the C2 server and saves the response to a memory mapped file named SNFIRNW. In addition to being able to communicate with its C2 server from code injected into a web browser, the Trojan can also carry out the same communication process within its own process. ATT&CK techniques observed: T1037. Tactic categories: Persistence, Privilege Escalation. Targeted sectors: Defense, Government, Legal. Delivery method(s): attachment, document, email, macro, phishing, website. Tools/frameworks observed: certutil, powershell, python, rundll32.",APT28,gold,cyber,G0007,Turla,29461750501a
