"In much the same way SierraJuliett- MikeOne and DeltaCharlie do not execute commands that have a lower command number than the last command they execute, RomeoMike ignores any command file with a lower command identifier number. Execute a command via the command line: {specified command} {output file} Execute Shell cmd.exe /c > 2>&1 Command ▲ ▲ ▲ ▲ ▲ The output file is a file located in the directory with Output %TEMP% having the name {random number} or Upload PM .tmp {random number} . It was possible, however, to reconstruct the majority of the command file set by enumerating all command files from all nodes and identify unique, valid command files. Targeted sectors: Media, Mining. Delivery method(s): email, rdp, usb. Tools/frameworks observed: cmd, ftp, netsh, netstat, tasklist.",Lazarus Group,gold,cyber,G0032,APT28,21266449e326
